espeak-ng 1.53.0, with pcaudiolib
Built from two upstream projects; both are GNU GPL version 3 or later.

  espeak-ng   https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng
              Source commit: ba90c8e9f440ad544f674a790bb5f53878b6ffc5 (2026-09-22)
              Unmodified - not one file of it was patched.

  pcaudiolib  https://github.com/espeak-ng/pcaudiolib
              Source commit: d6a6b00aa4334b461c1a09c27b6c681eaac8da8a (2018-03-10)
              Patched: a TinyALSA backend was added, since this board has no
              PulseAudio, ALSA, QSA or OSS.  The patch is three hunks and is
              shipped in the corresponding-source tree named below.

  TinyALSA    https://github.com/tinyalsa/tinyalsa
              Source commit: 961babfe962e71d952ae734074cc89576b28a9e7
              Licensed BSD-3-Clause; see TinyALSA-LICENSE. Include its source
              in the combined GPL binary's corresponding-source release.

The espeak-ng program and the compiled voice data in ../espeak-ng-data are
licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later; see COPYING.
The same licence covers pcaudiolib and the embedded TinyALSA backend; the text
is identical, and is also installed here as COPYING.PCAUDIOLIB so that the two
components can be told apart.  COPYING.APACHE, COPYING.BSD2 and COPYING.UCD
cover bundled components of espeak-ng.

This copy is an optional add-on for the N32H787 (ARMv7-M, no-MMU) board.  It is
cross-compiled with the SDK toolchain in sdk/toolchain/ and is deliberately not
part of any rootfs, of make, or of the SPI NOR images.

Corresponding source, as required by GPL-3.0 section 6:

  * The build glue for this specific binary is in the repository tree next to
    this drop:

      sdk/optional-src/espeak-ng/     the Makefile, the hand-written config.h,
                                      compat/ and probe/
      sdk/optional-src/pcaudiolib/    the Makefile, config.h, the new
                                      tinyalsa.c, and the patch that adds it

    If you pass these binaries on, provide the complete corresponding source
    and build materials under the applicable GPLv3 section 6 option; a pointer
    to port glue alone is not sufficient.

  * Upstream espeak-ng, unmodified, is at
    https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng , commit ba90c8e9f440ad544f674a790bb5f53878b6ffc5 (2026-09-22).
    That repository holds both the program sources and the voice-data inputs
    (phsource/, dictsource/), which the data in ../espeak-ng-data comes from.

  * Upstream pcaudiolib is at https://github.com/espeak-ng/pcaudiolib ,
    commit d6a6b00aa4334b461c1a09c27b6c681eaac8da8a (2018-03-10); apply
    sdk/optional-src/pcaudiolib/pcaudiolib-tinyalsa-backend.patch to it to get
    exactly the library that is linked into this binary.
